# Working style for new features

- Build the minimal viable version first: the least code that shows the idea works.
- Verify by rendering with the CLI (`drawland map <profile.js> -o out.svg`, then `rsvg-convert` to PNG) and show the image to the user. The user judges whether it looks right.
- Do not write large test suites or graphical comparison tests while iterating. Add tests only when the user asks or the feature is settled.
- Do not rebuild WASM, the web app, or the Python/Node bindings while iterating. Do that once the feature is accepted.
- Small steps; commit only when asked.
